 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Pullback of locally constant sheaves",
 "statement": "Let $g\\colon Y\\to X$ be a morphism and let $\\mathcal F\\in\\shv{\\et X}$ be\nlocally constant. Then $g^*\\mathcal F$ is locally constant.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-proper-base-change/sk-thm-p1/lemma-constructible-pullback-locally-constant.md",
  "place": "node lemma-constructible-pullback-locally-constant, order 1162"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-constructible-constant",
  "def-constructible-locally-constant"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Let $(U_i\\to X)_i$ be a trivialising datum for $\\mathcal F$. The base\nchange $(U_i\\times_XY\\to Y)_i$ is an étale cover of $Y$, since étale\nmorphisms and jointly surjective families are stable under base change.\nThe restriction of $g^*\\mathcal F$ to $\\et{U_i\\times_XY}$ is the pullback,\nalong the projection $g_i\\colon U_i\\times_XY\\to U_i$, of the restriction\nof $\\mathcal F$ to $\\et{U_i}$: pullback along $g$ followed by restriction to\nthe localised site equals restriction followed by pullback along $g_i$,\nbecause both are the sheaf pullback along the composite of the base change\nfunctors, which agree. The restriction of $\\mathcal F$ to $\\et{U_i}$ is\nconstant, and pullbacks of constant sheaves are constant by\n[lemma-constructible-pullback-constant]. Hence\n$(U_i\\times_XY\\to Y)_i$ is a trivialising datum for $g^*\\mathcal F$.",
   "uses": [
    "lemma-constructible-pullback-constant"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
